        "original_id": "352c8573-da40-5552-b696-d76cd77ef095",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: George Draper Dayton, Wallace L. Dow\n- Places: Worthington, Minnesota, United States\n- Buildings: George Draper Dayton House\n- Companies: Dayton's department store, Target Corporation\n\nFacts:\n- George Draper Dayton was born on March 6, 1857.\n- The George Draper Dayton House was built in 1890 in Worthington, Minnesota, United States.\n- George Draper Dayton hired Sioux Falls architect Wallace L. Dow to design the George Draper Dayton House on a parcel covering eight lots.\n- George Draper Dayton was an American businessman and philanthropist.\n- George Draper Dayton founded Dayton's department store, which later became Target Corporation.\n- George Draper Dayton died on February 18, 1938.",
